{"format":"bench-library","formatVersion":1,"id":"color-camera","name":"Colour-tracking camera","version":"1.0.0","author":"Bench Workshop","owner":"codeopen0-cpu","needsApp":"0.2.1","description":"A small camera that finds the biggest patch of one colour (red, green, blue, yellow...) in what it sees and tells a board where it is over I2C, like the Pixy or HuskyLens cameras robots use. A screen on its back shows what it sees. Includes BlobCam.h for sketches.","category":"Sensors","code":"// A colour-tracking camera: it looks at the bench through its \"eye\" camera, finds the pixels of the\n// colour it's tracking, and reports where they are over I2C, like a Pixy or HuskyLens.\n//\n// How it sees: part.camera('eye') gives pictures (80 x 60 RGBA) of the bench from its lens, 15 a\n// second. For each picture: every pixel whose hue is close to the target's (and that is colourful and\n// bright enough to tell) counts as \"found\"; their middle is the target's position.\n//\n// I2C (address 0x54): write [0x00] then read 6 bytes: found (0/1), x (0-255, left to right),\n// y (0-255, top to bottom), width, height (0-255), size (how much of the picture it fills, 0-255).\n// Write [0x10, r, g, b] to track another colour.\nbench.device('blobcam', (part) => {\n  const eye = part.camera('eye');\n  const view = part.screen('view');\n  const addr = Number(part.params.addr ?? 0x54);\n  let powered = false, pointer = 0, frames = 0, lastFrame = -1;\n  let target = hsv(255, 0, 0); // red to start with\n  const found = { yes: 0, x: 128, y: 128, w: 0, h: 0, size: 0 };\n\n  function hsv(r, g, b) {\n    const mx = Math.max(r, g, b), mn = Math.min(r, g, b), d = mx - mn;\n    let h = 0;\n    if (d) h = mx === r ? ((g - b) / d) % 6 : mx === g ? (b - r) / d + 2 : (r - g) / d + 4;\n    return { h: (h * 60 + 360) % 360, s: mx ? d / mx : 0, v: mx / 255 };\n  }\n  const hueGap = (a, b) => Math.min(Math.abs(a - b), 360 - Math.abs(a - b));\n\n  /** look at a new picture: where is the colour? and draw it on the back screen */\n  function analyse(f) {\n    let n = 0, sx = 0, sy = 0, x0 = f.width, y0 = f.height, x1 = -1, y1 = -1;\n    const hit = new Uint8Array(f.width * f.height);\n    for (let y = 0; y < f.height; y++)\n      for (let x = 0; x < f.width; x++) {\n        const i = (y * f.width + x) * 4;\n        const c = hsv(f.data[i], f.data[i + 1], f.data[i + 2]);\n        if (c.s > 0.45 && c.v > 0.2 && hueGap(c.h, target.h) < 22) {\n          hit[y * f.width + x] = 1;\n          n++; sx += x; sy += y;\n          if (x < x0) x0 = x; if (x > x1) x1 = x; if (y < y0) y0 = y; if (y > y1) y1 = y;\n        }\n      }\n    const min = Math.max(3, (f.width * f.height) / 1500); // a few pixels of noise isn't a find\n    found.yes = n >= min ? 1 : 0;\n    if (found.yes) {\n      found.x = Math.round(((sx / n) / (f.width - 1)) * 255);\n      found.y = Math.round(((sy / n) / (f.height - 1)) * 255);\n      found.w = Math.round(((x1 - x0 + 1) / f.width) * 255);\n      found.h = Math.round(((y1 - y0 + 1) / f.height) * 255);\n      found.size = Math.min(255, Math.round((n / (f.width * f.height)) * 255 * 4));\n    } else found.size = 0;\n    // the back screen: what it sees (32 x 24), what it found brighter, and a cross on the target\n    const cx = found.yes ? Math.round((found.x / 255) * (view.cols - 1)) : -1, cy = found.yes ? Math.round((found.y / 255) * (view.rows - 1)) : -1;\n    for (let sy2 = 0; sy2 < view.rows; sy2++)\n      for (let sx2 = 0; sx2 < view.cols; sx2++) {\n        const px = Math.floor(((sx2 + 0.5) / view.cols) * f.width), py = Math.floor(((sy2 + 0.5) / view.rows) * f.height);\n        const [r, g, b] = f.get(px, py);\n        const isHit = hit[py * f.width + px];\n        const k = isHit ? 1 : 0.55;\n        let col = `rgb(${Math.round(r * k)},${Math.round(g * k)},${Math.round(b * k)})`;\n        if ((sx2 === cx && Math.abs(sy2 - cy) <= 2) || (sy2 === cy && Math.abs(sx2 - cx) <= 2)) col = '#ffffff';\n        view.set(sx2, sy2, col);\n      }\n  }\n\n  return {\n    i2c: {\n      address: () => (powered ? addr : -1),\n      write(bytes) {\n        if (!bytes.length) return true;\n        pointer = bytes[0];\n        if (bytes[0] === 0x10 && bytes.length >= 4) {\n          target = hsv(bytes[1], bytes[2], bytes[3]);\n          part.log(`tracking hue ${Math.round(target.h)}`);\n        }\n        return true;\n      },\n      read(n) {\n        const regs = [found.yes, found.x, found.y, found.w, found.h, found.size];\n        const out = [];\n        for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) out.push(regs[pointer + i] ?? 0);\n        return out;\n      },\n    },\n    step(io) {\n      const now = io.supply('VCC', 'GND') >= 3.0;\n      if (now !== powered) {\n        powered = now;\n        eye.want(powered ? 15 : 0); // pictures only while it has power (15 a second: the most a camera gets)\n        view.light(powered);\n        if (!powered) view.fill(0);\n      }\n      const f = eye.frame;\n      if (powered && f && f.time !== lastFrame) {\n        lastFrame = f.time;\n        frames++;\n        analyse(f);\n      }\n    },\n    status() {\n      if (!powered) return ['no power (VCC 3.3-5 V)'];\n      if (!frames) return ['starting its camera...'];\n      return [found.yes ? `sees it at x ${found.x}, y ${found.y} (filling ${Math.round((found.size / 255) * 25)}% of the view)` : 'nothing of that colour in view', `${frames} pictures`];\n    },\n  };\n});\n","sketch":{"BlobCam.h":{"classes":["BlobCam"],"code":"// BlobCam for sketches: talks to the colour-tracking camera over I2C (Wire).\n//   BlobCam cam;              (or BlobCam cam(0x55); for the other address)\n//   cam.begin();\n//   cam.setColor(255, 0, 0);  the colour to track (red)\n//   if (cam.read() && cam.found) { cam.x, cam.y (0-255), cam.width, cam.height, cam.size }\nclass BlobCam {\n  constructor(addr = 0x54) {\n    this.addr = addr;\n    this.found = false;\n    this.x = 128;\n    this.y = 128;\n    this.width = 0;\n    this.height = 0;\n    this.size = 0;\n  }\n  begin() {\n    Wire.begin();\n    Wire.beginTransmission(this.addr);\n    return Wire.endTransmission() === 0; // true if the camera answered\n  }\n  setColor(r, g, b) {\n    Wire.beginTransmission(this.addr);\n    Wire.write(0x10);\n    Wire.write(r);\n    Wire.write(g);\n    Wire.write(b);\n    return Wire.endTransmission() === 0;\n  }\n  /** ask what it sees now; false if the camera didn't answer */\n  read() {\n    Wire.beginTransmission(this.addr);\n    Wire.write(0x00);\n    if (Wire.endTransmission() !== 0) return false;\n    if (Wire.requestFrom(this.addr, 6) !== 6) return false;\n    this.found = Wire.read() === 1;\n    this.x = Wire.read();\n    this.y = Wire.read();\n    this.width = Wire.read();\n    this.height = Wire.read();\n    this.size = Wire.read();\n    return true;\n  }\n}\n"}},"parts":[{"id":"blobcam","name":"Colour-tracking camera","description":"Looks along its lens (the +x side). VCC 3.3-5 V, GND, SDA, SCL; I2C address 0x54. In a sketch: #include <BlobCam.h>, BlobCam cam; cam.begin(); cam.setColor(255, 0, 0); then if (cam.read() && cam.found) use cam.x (0 = left edge, 255 = right), cam.y, cam.size. The screen on its back shows its view, with a cross on what it found.","swatch":"#2a6fd6","mass":8,"params":[{"key":"addr","label":"I2C address","kind":"select","options":[{"value":"84","label":"0x54"},{"value":"85","label":"0x55"}]}],"defaults":{"addr":"84"},"shape":[{"box":[1,2.6,3],"at":[0,1.3,0],"color":"#2a6fd6"},{"cyl":[0.55,0.5],"at":[0.75,1.6,0],"rot":[0,0,90],"color":"#151618"},{"cyl":[0.35,0.52],"at":[0.77,1.6,0],"rot":[0,0,90],"color":"#3a4a7a","collide":false},{"screen":{"id":"view","size":[2.6,1.95],"px":[32,24],"dots":false,"bg":"#000000","off":"#000000"},"at":[-0.505,1.4,0],"rot":[90,0,90]},{"camera":{"id":"eye","px":[80,60],"fov":55,"look":[1,0,0],"range":600},"at":[1.05,1.6,0]}],"pinRows":[{"ids":["VCC","GND","SDA","SCL"],"at":[-0.75,0,-0.381],"dir":"z","header":false,"kinds":{"VCC":"vin","GND":"gnd","SDA":"i2c","SCL":"i2c"},"extra":{"VCC":{"label":"VCC (3.3-5 V)","vmin":3,"vmax":5.5}}}],"device":"blobcam"}],"examples":[{"name":"Rover chases a red ball","description":"A rover with the camera on its nose turns towards a red ball, drives to it and stops in front of it. Move the ball (drag it while running) and it follows.","project":{"format":"bench-workshop","version":1,"name":"Rover chases a red ball","libraries":[{"id":"color-camera","name":"Colour-tracking camera","version":"1.0.0"}],"parts":[{"uid":"chassis","type":"plate","name":"Chassis","params":{"w":12,"h":0.3,"d":9,"material":"plastic","color":"#8fa3b8"},"parent":null,"pos":[0,4.4,0],"rot":[0,0,0,1]},{"uid":"motorR","type":"motor-tt","name":"Right motor","params":{},"parent":{"uid":"chassis","body":"body"},"pos":[0,-0.15,3.55],"rot":[0,0,1,0]},{"uid":"motorL","type":"motor-tt","name":"Left motor","params":{},"parent":{"uid":"chassis","body":"body"},"pos":[3.2,-0.15,-3.55],"rot":[1,0,0,0]},{"uid":"wheelR","type":"wheel","name":"Right wheel","params":{"r":3.3,"width":2.6,"grip":1.2},"parent":{"uid":"motorR","body":"hub"},"pos":[0,0.45,0],"rot":[0,1,0,0]},{"uid":"wheelL","type":"wheel","name":"Left wheel","params":{"r":3.3,"width":2.6,"grip":1.2},"parent":{"uid":"motorL","body":"hub"},"pos":[0,0.45,0],"rot":[0,0,0,1]},{"uid":"caster","type":"caster","name":"Caster","params":{"r":1.57},"parent":{"uid":"chassis","body":"body"},"pos":[-4.6,-0.15,0],"rot":[0,0,1,0]},{"uid":"battery","type":"battery-18650","name":"Batteries (2x 18650, 7.4 V)","params":{"count":"2","charge":100},"parent":{"uid":"chassis","body":"body"},"pos":[-2.2,0.15,0],"rot":[0,0,0,1]},{"uid":"brain","type":"maker-board","name":"Brain","params":{"usb":false},"parent":{"uid":"chassis","body":"body"},"pos":[2.6,0.15,0],"rot":[0,-0.7071,0,0.7071]},{"uid":"driver","type":"drv8833","name":"Motor driver","params":{},"parent":{"uid":"battery","body":"body"},"pos":[0,2,0],"rot":[0,0,0,1]},{"uid":"camera","type":"color-camera/blobcam","name":"Camera","params":{"addr":"84"},"parent":{"uid":"chassis","body":"body"},"pos":[5.2,0.15,0],"rot":[0,0,0,1]},{"uid":"ball","type":"ball","name":"Red ball","params":{"r":3,"material":"plastic","color":"#e02828"},"parent":null,"pos":[55,0,-28],"rot":[0,0,0,1]}],"wires":[{"id":"w1","a":{"uid":"battery","pin":"+"},"b":{"uid":"driver","pin":"VM"},"color":"#e04848"},{"id":"w2","a":{"uid":"battery","pin":"-"},"b":{"uid":"driver","pin":"GND"},"color":"#2b2d33"},{"id":"w3","a":{"uid":"battery","pin":"+"},"b":{"uid":"brain","pin":"VIN"},"color":"#e04848"},{"id":"w4","a":{"uid":"battery","pin":"-"},"b":{"uid":"brain","pin":"GND2"},"color":"#2b2d33"},{"id":"w5","a":{"uid":"brain","pin":"GP2"},"b":{"uid":"driver","pin":"AIN1"},"color":"#4f9cff"},{"id":"w6","a":{"uid":"brain","pin":"GP3"},"b":{"uid":"driver","pin":"AIN2"},"color":"#4f9cff"},{"id":"w7","a":{"uid":"brain","pin":"GP5"},"b":{"uid":"driver","pin":"BIN1"},"color":"#3fbf7f"},{"id":"w8","a":{"uid":"brain","pin":"GP6"},"b":{"uid":"driver","pin":"BIN2"},"color":"#3fbf7f"},{"id":"w9","a":{"uid":"driver","pin":"AOUT1"},"b":{"uid":"motorR","pin":"M+"},"color":"#e8c547"},{"id":"w10","a":{"uid":"driver","pin":"AOUT2"},"b":{"uid":"motorR","pin":"M-"},"color":"#ff9d3a"},{"id":"w11","a":{"uid":"driver","pin":"BOUT1"},"b":{"uid":"motorL","pin":"M+"},"color":"#e8c547"},{"id":"w12","a":{"uid":"driver","pin":"BOUT2"},"b":{"uid":"motorL","pin":"M-"},"color":"#ff9d3a"},{"id":"c1","a":{"uid":"brain","pin":"3V3"},"b":{"uid":"camera","pin":"VCC"},"color":"#e04848"},{"id":"c2","a":{"uid":"brain","pin":"GND"},"b":{"uid":"camera","pin":"GND"},"color":"#2b2d33"},{"id":"c3","a":{"uid":"brain","pin":"SDA"},"b":{"uid":"camera","pin":"SDA"},"color":"#4f9cff"},{"id":"c4","a":{"uid":"brain","pin":"SCL"},"b":{"uid":"camera","pin":"SCL"},"color":"#e8c547"}],"programs":{"brain":{"lang":"arduino","source":"// Rover chases a red ball: the colour-tracking camera on its nose says where red is in its view;\n// the rover turns towards it, drives up to it and stops when it fills the view. Drag the ball\n// somewhere else while it runs and it goes after it. Nothing red in view: it turns on the spot to look.\n#include <BlobCam.h>\n\n#define AIN1 2    // right motor, through the DRV8833\n#define AIN2 3\n#define BIN1 5    // left motor\n#define BIN2 6\n\nBlobCam cam;\n\nvoid motor(int in1, int in2, int speed) {\n  speed = constrain(speed, -255, 255);\n  if (speed >= 0) { analogWrite(in1, speed); analogWrite(in2, 0); }\n  else            { analogWrite(in1, 0);     analogWrite(in2, -speed); }\n}\n\nvoid drive(int left, int right) {   // -255 .. 255\n  motor(BIN1, BIN2, left);\n  motor(AIN2, AIN1, right);         // the right motor faces the other way\n}\n\nvoid setup() {\n  Serial.begin(115200);\n  if (!cam.begin()) Serial.println(\"no camera on I2C: check its wires\");\n  cam.setColor(255, 0, 0);          // look for red\n  Serial.println(\"looking for red\");\n}\n\nvoid loop() {\n  if (cam.read() && cam.found) {\n    int err = cam.x - 128;              // how far from the middle (left: negative)\n    if (cam.size > 140) {\n      drive(0, 0);                      // it fills the view: we are there\n      Serial.println(\"got it!\");\n    } else if (abs(err) > 40) {\n      // off to one side: turn on the spot towards it, slower as it nears the middle\n      // (turning fast overshoots: the camera only looks 15 times a second)\n      int t = constrain(err / 2, -75, 75);\n      if (t > 0 && t < 55) t = 55;      // below this the gearbox won't turn\n      if (t < 0 && t > -55) t = -55;\n      drive(t, -t);\n    } else {\n      int speed = 160 - cam.size * 3 / 4; // slower as it gets closer (bigger in the view)\n      if (speed < 70) speed = 70;\n      drive(speed + err / 2, speed - err / 2); // roughly ahead: drive, steering a little\n    }\n  } else {\n    drive(60, -60);                     // nothing red in view: turn slowly and look\n  }\n  delay(30);\n}\n"}},"boards":[]}}]}